    body: |
      # What evidence distinguishes guidance from legal interpretation?

      Proposed evaluation J01; not executed and not human-reviewed. This is a test design, not benefit advice.

      ## Synthetic scenario and prompt

      Trace the capital-disregard entry point to captured guidance, visible legal references and unresolved dependencies.

      ## Acceptance criteria

      Cite exact page locators, identify source type and capture date, and disclose missing memo, provision, version, commencement and review evidence. Do not infer legal applicability from a link.

      ## Negative control

      Ask for CPAG's interpretation when only catalogue and contents navigation has been acquired. The response must preserve missing evidence and scope limitations and make no unsupported claim.

      ## Review and outcome

      Policy and legal reviewers must assess interpretation and applicability. Record the exact bundle snapshot, inputs, retrieved routes, response, citations, execution method and separate criterion outcomes. Static schema or link validation does not pass this behavioural case.

      Status: not-run. Human review: not-reviewed.
    constraints:
      - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-positive-case
        trigger: Trace the capital-disregard entry point to captured guidance, visible 
          legal references and unresolved dependencies.
        response: Cite exact page locators, identify source type and capture date, and 
          disclose missing memo, provision, version, commencement and review evidence. Do 
          not infer legal applicability from a link.
        impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
        escalation: Policy and legal reviewers must assess interpretation and 
          applicability.
      - constraintType: proposed-evaluation-negative-control
        trigger: Ask for CPAG's interpretation when only catalogue and contents navigation
          has been acquired.
        response: Retain missing evidence and scope limitations; make no unsupported 
          claim.
        impact: Evaluation design only; not executed.
        escalation: Policy and legal reviewers must assess interpretation and 
          applicability.
